      "Saint Shallita (Artemius)": 1,
      "Shallita, also known as Artemius, was born in the fourth century. A high-ranking Roman army officer, he was given responsibility for the troops stationed in Egypt and remained a faithful Christian despite the danger to his position and his life. Summoned before the emperor in Antioch for destroying pagan temples and idols, he is held in great veneration. Many churches and monasteries in Lebanon bear his name, and he is considered the patron of animals.": 1,
      "Brief story based on the Eparchy of Saint Maron of Brooklyn feast-day article.": 1,
